<workflow>
  <name>main-0057-insert-update-batch-error-accounting</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>Insert/Update with an error hop on SQL Server 2022 (Microsoft driver), fourteen rows at commit size 5 on a table that holds the even ids, so inserts and updates interleave; three of them are refused by a check constraint: an update in the middle of the first commit window, an insert at the first position of the second and an insert in the final partial window. A row needs no change, and a key comes twice in the final window. Once with batch updates on: the driver's validated batch failure contract (it runs the whole batch and marks the failed rows) tells which rows of a failed batch were refused, and the waiting key writes the batches before it is looked up again. Once with batch updates off: every row is inserted or updated on its own and passed on right after it, as before. Asserts for both that exactly the three bad rows reach the error stream, with the error code of their path, that the good rows are committed and reported once, and that the table ends up the same.</description>
  <extended_description/>
  <workflow_version/>
  <created_user>-</created_user>
  <created_date>2026/11/27 12:00:00.000</created_date>
  <modified_user>-</modified_user>
